MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: SW V7.1 cached /api/* responses under cache 'voy-v7-1'. During the
brief 'Observer' Next.js build era on the same Worker, RSC streaming payloads
('data: {...}') got stored. After VOY V7.8.0 redeploy, SW kept serving those
stale cached responses, causing SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'd', "data: {\"da\"..."
in the frontend (HIGH_UI_BREAKING, confidence 0.94 client-side state corruption).

SW V7.1 -> V7.2:
- Bumped cache name 'voy-v7-1' -> 'voy-v7-2' (forces fresh start)
- Activate handler purges ALL caches unconditionally (was: non-matching only)
- /api/* paths NEVER intercepted by SW (passthrough to network)
- Respect req.cache === 'no-store' (skip caching)
- Respect response Cache-Control: no-store|no-cache (skip caching)
- All V7.1 behavior preserved: navigations network-first, unpkg CDN cache-first,
  static assets stale-while-revalidate, cross-origin passthrough

Backend NOT modified: all 14 endpoint paths verified clean JSON (no 'data:' prefix
anywhere in codebase — 0 matches for SSE/streaming patterns).

Also includes:
- scripts/watch-isadev-pr.py + .github/workflows/watch-isadev-pr.yml: autonomous
  monitor for is-a-dev/register PR #41619 (every 12h cron, issue-on-change).
- .gitignore: add prod-*.png + tool-results/ to prevent future artifact contamination.
